  "id": "high-threshold",
  "term": "high threshold",
  "definition": "In this context, high threshold refers to relatively lower sensitivity to mechanical pain, meaning a stronger stimulus is needed before pain is perceived compared with a low-threshold group. It is used to describe differences in pain sensitivity between people.",
